  "`" markup.list.numbered.markdown meta.paragraph.markdown markup.inline.raw.string.markdown punctuation.definition.raw.markdown
  "user:" markup.list.numbered.markdown meta.paragraph.markdown markup.inline.raw.string.markdown
  "`" markup.list.numbered.markdown meta.paragraph.markdown markup.inline.raw.string.markdown punctuation.definition.raw.markdown
  "`" markup.list.numbered.markdown meta.paragraph.markdown markup.inline.raw.string.markdown punctuation.definition.raw.markdown
  "agent:" markup.list.numbered.markdown meta.paragraph.markdown markup.inline.raw.string.markdown
  "`" markup.list.numbered.markdown meta.paragraph.markdown markup.inline.raw.string.markdown punctuation.definition.raw.markdown
>    two sources is two entries, even when they land in the same edit.
> 3. **A person's input is recorded faithfully, first.** When a person gives direction, the first
  "3." markup.list.numbered.markdown punctuation.definition.list.begin.markdown
  "**" markup.list.numbered.markdown meta.paragraph.markdown markup.bold.markdown punctuation.definition.bold.markdown
  "A person's input is recorded faithfully, first." markup.list.numbered.markdown meta.paragraph.markdown markup.bold.markdown
  "**" markup.list.numbered.markdown meta.paragraph.markdown markup.bold.markdown punctuation.definition.bold.markdown
>    entry is `by: user:<them>` and says what they said — nothing more. `quote:` carries their words
  "`" markup.list.numbered.markdown meta.paragraph.markdown markup.inline.raw.string.markdown punctuation.definition.raw.markdown
  "by: user:<them>" markup.list.numbered.markdown meta.paragraph.markdown markup.inline.raw.string.markdown
  "`" markup.list.numbered.markdown meta.paragraph.markdown markup.inline.raw.string.markdown punctuation.definition.raw.markdown
  "`" markup.list.numbered.markdown meta.paragraph.markdown markup.inline.raw.string.markdown punctuation.definition.raw.markdown
  "quote:" markup.list.numbered.markdown meta.paragraph.markdown markup.inline.raw.string.markdown
  "`" markup.list.numbered.markdown meta.paragraph.markdown markup.inline.raw.string.markdown punctuation.definition.raw.markdown
>    verbatim. `context:` may add facts that make the entry readable on its own (what a name refers
  "`" markup.list.numbered.markdown meta.paragraph.markdown markup.inline.raw.string.markdown punctuation.definition.raw.markdown
  "context:" markup.list.numbered.markdown meta.paragraph.markdown markup.inline.raw.string.markdown
  "`" markup.list.numbered.markdown meta.paragraph.markdown markup.inline.raw.string.markdown punctuation.definition.raw.markdown
>    to, where it was said); it adds no requirement, no rationale they did not give, and no
>    assumption. The decider is who chose, not who typed: an agent writes this entry, the person
>    made it.
> 4. **What the agent adds is a separate entry.** Gaps the agent filled — shapes, names, edge cases,
  "4." markup.list.numbered.markdown punctuation.definition.list.begin.markdown
  "**" markup.list.numbered.markdown meta.paragraph.markdown markup.bold.markdown punctuation.definition.bold.markdown
